In .NET 10 (and Android 15+), `adjustResize` is deprecated. MAUI now uses **edge-to-edge** mode by default, and you handle keyboard insets via the new `KeyboardInsets` API or by enabling the compatibility flag.

### Quick Fix — Compatibility Flag

In your `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder
    .UseMauiApp<App>()
    .ConfigureMauiHandlers(handlers =>
    {
#if ANDROID
        // Opt back into legacy resize behavior
        Microsoft.Maui.Handlers.WindowHandler.Mapper.AppendToMapping(
            "AdjustResize", (handler, view) =>
            {
                var activity = handler.PlatformView;
                activity.Window?.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(true);
            });
#endif
    });
```

### Recommended Approach — Edge-to-Edge with Padding

The proper fix is to let the OS report keyboard height and adjust your layout:

```xml
<!-- ChatPage.xaml -->
<Grid RowDefinitions="*, Auto">
    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" x:Name="Messages" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />
    <HorizontalStackLayout Grid.Row="1" x:Name="InputBar" Padding="8">
        <Entry Placeholder="Type a message..." HorizontalOptions="FillAndExpand" />
        <Button Text="Send" />
    </HorizontalStackLayout>
</Grid>
```

```csharp
// ChatPage.xaml.cs (Android-specific inset handling)
#if ANDROID
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui.Platform;

// In OnAppearing or constructor after InitializeComponent:
var activity = Platform.CurrentActivity;
var rootView = activity?.Window?.DecorView?.RootView;
if (rootView is not null)
{
    ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(rootView, new InsetsListener(InputBar));
}

class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
{
    private readonly View _target;
    public InsetsListener(View target) => _target = target;

    public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
    {
        var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
        _target.Margin = new Thickness(0, 0, 0, imeInsets.Bottom /
            DeviceDisplay.MainDisplayInfo.Density);
        return insets;
    }
}
#endif
```

### Key Takeaways

| | .NET 9 | .NET 10+ |
|---|---|---|
| **API** | `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` | `WindowInsetsCompat` / edge-to-edge |
| **Why** | Android 15 deprecated `adjustResize` | OS now reports insets; apps respond |

The **compatibility flag** is fastest to ship, but the **insets approach** is forward-proof and gives you precise control over which views move.
